[{"id":5226300837,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABN4MFpQ","user":{"login":"vedant21-oss","id":210591514,"node_id":"U_kgDODI1fGg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/210591514?u=5ebe737af1b8ea7f167247794318edac66deda73&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss","html_url":"https://github.com/vedant21-oss","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vedant21-oss/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a really nice change, the guessing has bitten a few rules already. I built it and ran the tool tests locally and everything passes. Two things I ran into while playing with it:","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/1312#pullrequestreview-5226300837","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/1312","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/1312#pullrequestreview-5226300837"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/1312"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-16T17:51:11Z","commit_id":"c08fda94615fed95cfb78ca58d28961f8c7f3684"},{"id":5234164676,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABN_sDxA","user":{"login":"om7057","id":127368012,"node_id":"U_kgDOB5d7TA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/127368012?u=4cca4ebfe694346ad0ce573bead9753979e23c35&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057","html_url":"https://github.com/om7057","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/om7057/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is a substantially larger change than the others I've reviewed recently, roughly thirty files, most of it test coverage, so I gave it a correspondingly closer look before commenting.\n\nPulled the branch down, and it builds and vets cleanly. I did hit test failures on the first run, but traced each one back to my own environment rather than the PR. The `tool/internal/setup` failures come from real `go mod tidy` invocations hitting a corporate proxy that isn't reachable from here, and a couple of `pkgload` path-comparison tests failed due to a `GOTMPDIR` I had set with mixed slash conventions. I confirmed both by running the same tests against unpatched `main` and getting identical failures there, so neither is attributable to this change. With the environment corrected, `ast`, `instrument`, and `pkgload` all pass without issue.\n\nRather than take the motivating bug on faith, I wrote a small standalone test against `ImportAliasMap` using an unaliased `github.com/redis/go-redis/v9` import. Without the resolved-names table, it guesses `go-redis`, the incorrect name described in the PR. Supplying the resolved name correctly returns `redis`. That confirms the core fix behaves as claimed.\n\nThe overall design holds together well. `CollectPackageNames` builds the import-path-to-package-name table once during setup by walking the dependency graph, persists it to `import_names.json`, and the instrument phase reads it back without needing a second `go/packages` load, which the code comments correctly note would be too expensive to repeat per compile process. The `resolveAliasOverrides`/`replaceQualifierAliases` handling for a file that already imports a path under a different alias is a genuine improvement as well; that case previously failed the build outright and now rewrites the generated code to match. The relocation of `usedRuleImports` from `apply_call.go` into the shared `imports.go` is a straightforward deduplication with no behavioral change.\n","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/1312#pullrequestreview-5234164676","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/1312","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pull/1312#pullrequestreview-5234164676"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-compile-instrumentation/pulls/1312"}},"submitted_at":"2026-09-17T10:15:36Z","commit_id":"c08fda94615fed95cfb78ca58d28961f8c7f3684"},{"id":5255704321,"node_id":"PRR_kwDONpzSS88AAAABOUOvAQ","user":{"login":"ADITYA-CODE-SOURCE","id":181550800,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtI-0A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181550800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-CODE-SOURCE","html_url":"https://github.com/ADITYA-CODE-SOURCE","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ADITYA-CODE-SOURCE/followers","